From: Shital Shah <2096835+sytelus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 21:53:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] backend: wsl, a remote-viewer backend

A backend for compositors running where there is no display hardware but a viewer elsewhere shows
the outputs (written for WSL2 with omarchy.exe, but generic): it listens on AF_VSOCK (or a unix
socket), authenticates the viewer with a token, creates one output per viewer monitor, and sends
frames as damage rectangles over WDP (womarchy display protocol, src/backend/wsl/wdp.h) - either by
reference to shm files the viewer maps itself, or inline. Frames are paced by the viewer's acks;
keyboard, pointer and cursor images travel over the same socket. Monitor changes (add, remove,
resize) are applied live; an optional orphan timeout ends the session when no viewer returns.
CBackend::start falls back to the backend's own allocator when there is no DRM fd.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
