+    /*
+        The "wsl" backend drives a remote viewer (omarchy.exe on the Windows host of a WSL2 VM).
+        Outputs mirror the viewer's monitors; frames are CPU (shm) buffers the renderer reads back
+        into, announced to the viewer with their damage over a socket (AF_VSOCK <-> AF_HYPERV).
+        Pixels either live in files on WSLg's section-backed shared-memory share (zero copy) or are
+        sent inline. Input and cursor images travel over the same socket. See wsl/wdp.h.
+
+        Configuration (environment): WOMARCHY_TOKEN (64 hex chars, required), WOMARCHY_VSOCK_PORT or
+        WOMARCHY_LISTEN_UNIX, WOMARCHY_MONITORS, WOMARCHY_SHM_DIR, WOMARCHY_VM_ID,
+        WOMARCHY_ORPHAN_TIMEOUT (seconds), WOMARCHY_TRACE, WOMARCHY_SOFTWARE_CURSOR.
